         '(A stage play)\nCharacters: Dr Zaidi, Mrs Zaidi, Dr Burhan\nSetting: Dr Zaidi\'s room\n(The doctor sits on the bed leaning against a bolster. He is about forty-five, with a French-cut beard and visible weakness in his face; at the moment he is wrapped in a blanket. On a small table by the bed are various medicine bottles. It is a stormy night; a fierce wind is making a constant noise. Mrs Zaidi sits in an easy chair reading a magazine. She is about fifty and has a shawl round her against the cold. The doctor is lost in thought. Suddenly his eyes fall on the door opposite, which has a blue curtain over it. His wife looks at him and then goes back to turning the pages of her magazine. The doctor says something, but very softly; only his lips can be seen moving. Then he begins to push the blanket off. His wife notices.)',
